description:
Hi

While searching for other information in this package, I came across the function that reports the pandoc version. I’d like to clarify why we are using `isNamespaceLoaded()` and whether it might be preferable to check instead if {rmarkdown} is *installed*.

Here is an example that illustrates the reason for my question. Start in a **fresh** R session and run:

```
get_pandoc_version <- function() {
  if (isNamespaceLoaded("rmarkdown")) {
    ver <- rmarkdown::find_pandoc()
    if (is.null(ver$dir)) {
      "NA (via rmarkdown)"
    } else {
      paste0(ver$version, " @ ", ver$dir, "/ (via rmarkdown)")
    }
  } else {
    path <- Sys.which("pandoc")
    if (path == "") {
      "NA"
    } else {
      ver <- parse_pandoc_version(path)
      paste0(ver, " @ ", path)
    }
  }
}

parse_pandoc_version <- function(path) {
  tryCatch(
    {
      out <- system2(path, "--version", stdout = TRUE)[1]
      last(strsplit(out, " ", fixed = TRUE)[[1]])
    },
    error = function(e) "NA"
  )
}
```

Now, i.e., in a session where {rmarkdown} has not been loaded/attached:

```
> get_pandoc_version()
[1] "NA"
```

With and after calling `rmarkdown::find_pandoc()`:

```
> rmarkdown::find_pandoc()
$version
[1] ‘3.6.3’

$dir
[1] "c:\\Program Files\\Positron\\resources\\app\\quarto\\bin\\tools"
> get_pandoc_version()
[1] "3.6.3 @ c:\\Program Files\\Positron\\resources\\app\\quarto\\bin\\tools/ (via rmarkdown)"
````

Howdy! 

Would it be possible to return the `quarto` version as part of session info?

`pandoc` is currently reported, but would be great to also have the `quarto` version itself at the bottom of the Session Info section.

```
─ Session info ─────────────────────────
 setting  value
 version  R version 4.1.1 (2021-08-10)
 os       macOS Monterey 12.2.1
 system   aarch64, darwin20
 ui       RStudio
 language (EN)
 collate  en_US.UTF-8
 ctype    en_US.UTF-8
 tz       America/Chicago
 date     2022-04-18
 rstudio  2022.06.0-daily+217 Spotted Wakerobin (desktop)
 pandoc   2.17.1.1 @ /Applications/RStudio.app/Contents/MacOS/quarto/bin/ (via markdown)
```

A quick attempt at implementation based off the `get_pandoc_version()` function.

``` r
get_quarto_version <- function() {
  if (isNamespaceLoaded("quarto")) {
    path <- quarto::quarto_path()
    ver <- system("quarto -V", intern = TRUE)
    if (is.null(path)) {
      "NA (via quarto)"
    } else {
      paste0(ver, " @ ", path, "/ (via quarto)")
    }
  } else {
    path <- Sys.which("quarto")
    if (path == "") {
      "NA"
    } else {
      ver <- system("quarto -V", intern = TRUE)
      paste0(ver, " @ ", path)
    }
  }
}


get_quarto_version()
#> [1] "0.9.172 @ /usr/local/bin/quarto"
```

